=====Usage notes=====
Often used in {{w|phono-semantic matching}}s to translate English and German {{m|en|-burg}}, or English {{m|en|-burgh}}, etc.<br>
Some place names or surnames with the component {{m|de|Berg}} are also translated with {{l-self|zh|堡}}, but this is a result of confusion between {{m|de|Burg}} and {{m|de|Berg}}, with the latter meaning "mountain" instead of "castle". Nowadays {{m|de|Berg}} is usually transliterated as {{m|zh|[[貝]][[格]]}} or {{m|zh|[[伯]][[格]]}}, except in a few examples such as {{m|zh|紐倫堡|t=Nuremberg}}, {{m|zh|海德堡|t=Heidelberg}}, and {{m|zh|海森堡|t=Heisenberg}}.

